#### Interpretation

If the smoke test holds (~67% behavior flip), this is the wedge: token edits 0/20 versus free-form rewrites ~13/20 means the probe direction *can* be exploited from input space — but only with enough freedom to rewrite, not just nudge tokens. The probe captures something real that an attacker can reach, just not via the single-token attribution surface.

This complicates the Level-2A negative result. The probe is *not* purely correlational — there's a causal handle accessible from input space. It just isn't the handle the attribution map points at.

